    d.h1('11. Symbols that look alike')
    d.ul(['$\\beta$: the radion field $\\beta(x)$ (this document) and the constant $\\beta$ of the note’s ansatz; $\\beta_n$ the constant for $n$ extra '
          'dimensions. Our $\\beta(x)$ equals the note’s product $\\beta\\phi(x)$.',
          '$\\alpha$: the note’s constant in $e^{2\\alpha\\phi}$ and the strength $\\alpha$ of a Yukawa (fifth) force.',
          '$\\phi$, $\\varphi$, $\\varphi_H$, $\\Phi$: the canonical radion $\\phi$; the note’s dimensionless radion $\\varphi$; the radial Higgs field $\\varphi_H$; '
          'a bulk scalar $\\Phi$.',
          '$\\lambda$: the Higgs quartic coupling, the Dirac eigenvalue on $S^4$, the range of a Yukawa force, and (with subscripts) the note’s brane '
          'tensions.',
          '$\\epsilon$, $\\varepsilon$: the Goldberger–Wise parameter $\\epsilon=m^2/(4k^2)$; the energy density $\\varepsilon$; the Killing spinors $\\varepsilon_s$.',
          '$\\gamma$: the reference metric $\\gamma_{ij}$ ($\\hat\\gamma$ for the unit sphere), the Higgs–radion parameter $\\gamma=v/\\Lambda_r$, and the '
          'photon in $h\\to\\gamma\\gamma$; $\\tilde\\gamma_a$ are Dirac matrices.',
          '$\\sigma$: the curvature switch of $V(\\beta)$ and the divisor sum $\\sigma(k)$.',
          '$r$: the radius of the sphere, the distance between two masses, and the bare radion field $r(x)$; $r_m$ the radion mass eigenstate; '
          '$r_4(k)$ the lattice multiplicity.',
          '$h$: the induced metric $h_{\\mu\\nu}$, the bare Higgs field $h(x)$ and the mass eigenstate $h_m$.',
          '$R$: scalar curvature ($R$, $R_E$, $R_{\\rm int}$), the Randall–Sundrum radius $R$, and $R(h)$, the curvature of the induced metric.',
          '$K$: the stiffness $K_U$, the kinetic matrix $K$, the extrinsic curvature $K^\\mu{}_\\nu$.',
          '$f$: the brane tension $f$ ($f_{\\rm UV}$, $f_{\\rm IR}$), the normalization $f$ of the warped radion, and $f_W$ (the tension of the world brane of 7+1).',
          '$\\Lambda$, $\\Lambda_r$: the bulk cosmological constant; the coupling scale of the radion.',
          '$M$: a point mass, the Randall–Sundrum scale $M$, $M_5$, $M_8$, $M_{\\rm Pl}$, and the mass matrix $M\'$.',
          '$S$: the action $S$, the kinetic shift matrix $S$, the brane energy–momentum $S_{\\mu\\nu}$, the sphere $S^4$.',
          '$x$: the coordinates and the dimensionless $x=\\mu r$ of Weyl’s law; $y$: the extra coordinates, the fifth coordinate of RS1, and $y=L+2$.',
          '$Z$: the normalization $Z$ and the zonal harmonics $Z_l$; $\\mathbb Z$ the integers.',
          '$c$: the coefficient $c=-6$ and the coefficients $c_n$; $C_1$, $C_2$, $C_h$, $C_r$, $C_l^{(3/2)}$ are different objects.'])

